# agent-verify settings for this repo (committed; personal overrides go in .agent/verify.local.env).
# The presence of this file turns the web agent kit's hooks on for this repo. /web-onboard fills it in.

# BASE_BRANCH=main                     # default: origin/HEAD, then main/master
#                                      # (none of those? set it, or commits on a branch aren't seen as changes)
# SPECS_DIR=docs/specs                 # where /web-spec writes specs

# --- Checks (defaults are auto-detected per package from package.json scripts) -------------------
# fast: typecheck|type-check (or tsc --noEmit if tsconfig.json) + lint + test:unit|test in affected packages
# full: fast + build + test:property + test:mutation (where defined) + scanners
# JS_FAST_CMD="pnpm turbo run typecheck lint test --filter=...[origin/main]"   # replaces per-package fast
# JS_FULL_CMD="pnpm turbo run build --filter=...[origin/main]"                 # with JS_FAST_CMD, for full
# EXTRA_FAST_CMD="./scripts/check-something.sh"    # runs after the package checks in fast and full; its test
#                                                  # results count when it prints some, but it needn't
# INSTALL_CMD="pnpm install --frozen-lockfile"     # default from the lockfile. Not needed for agent worktrees:
#                                                  # they link the main checkout's node_modules when lockfiles match
# ENV_FALLBACK_FROM="apps/web/.env.example"        # for tools that read .env (CRA, Vite): these templates' values
#                                                  # are exported when the real .env is missing or hidden —
#                                                  # Claude Code's sandbox hides real .env files from commands
# REQUIRE_TESTS=1                      # default 1: every package's test step must print test results
# TEST_EVIDENCE_REGEX='...'            # if your runner's summary isn't recognized
# SKIP="mutation"                      # any of: lint test build mutation semgrep ruff gitleaks values
#                                      # (AGENT_VERIFY_SKIP=... for one run: it then writes no verify stamp)
# Steps run with CI=true, as in GitHub Actions: CRA 5, for one, fails the build on lint warnings. If the
# repo's CI sets CI=false somewhere, that is a real difference to fix, not one to copy here.

# --- e2e -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# E2E_COMPOSE=docker-compose.dev.yml   # started (docker compose up -d --wait) before e2e
# E2E_CMD="pnpm --filter student test:e2e"   # default: test:e2e in the root, else in affected packages
E2E_CMD="uv run pytest -m e2e"

# --- Change report (agent-verify diff) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# RISK_PATHS="billing=^apps/admin/src/billing/ ^packages/shared/src/grading"   # extra EREs, each optionally
#                                       # label=ERE (the report shows the label); defaults cover migrations,
#                                       # auth, access rules, API routes, env/config, CI, deploy config
# DIFF_CMD="pnpm --filter shared run api-diff"   # extra output appended to the report
# Flat Flask app: the defaults only catch render.yaml/Procfile/Dockerfile/.env.example here.
# app.py holds every route, the sign-in flow and every permission check.
RISK_PATHS="routes-auth-permissions=^app\.py$ schema-and-migrations=^(schema\.sql|db\.py)$ moderation=^(moderation\.py|blocked_words\.txt)$ photo-uploads=^photos\.py$ outbound-email=^mailer\.py$ dependencies=^requirements\.txt$"

# --- Tests, code you don't own, scanners -------------------------------------------------------------
# PROTECTED_TESTS="packages/shared/src/**/*.contract.test.ts"   # only these existing tests are locked
# VENDORED_PATHS="vendor/ apps/student/public/lib/"             # not scanned as yours; edits ask Trevor
# LOCAL_DB_HOSTS="devdb"               # extra hostnames the guard treats as local databases
# FAKE_IDS="123456789012"              # fake AWS account IDs allowed in code/tests/docs
# IDENTIFIER_PATTERNS='...'            # extra formats to flag in added lines
